  "question": {
    "text": "If the point <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies between the two different lines <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the least integral value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
