  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies between two different lines&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8746;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the least integral value of&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mn>3</mn></math></p>"
  }
